# Act structure. An act is a self-contained run of rooms with its own opening and closing
# cinematic; finishing one carries the inventory and flags forward and drops you into the next.

act 1 "A Licence to Sail"
  start dock
  intro "/assets/video/intro.mp4"
  outro "/assets/video/act-i-outro.mp4"
  inventory compass
  caption "Three years stamping other people's voyages. At dawn the Marrow sails for the Straits, where my father's ship vanished — and she only takes licensed hands."

act 2 "The Vela Straits"
  start marrow_deck
  intro "/assets/video/act-ii-intro.mp4"
  outro "/assets/video/act-ii-outro.mp4"
  inventory compass stamp manifest crowbar licence
  caption "Dawn, and the Marrow is mine to stand on. The crew have already decided what I am: a clerk with a licence and no sea legs. The compass in my pocket is still pointing somewhere that isn't north."

act 3 "Tidy Weather"
  start reef_wreck
  intro "/assets/video/act-iii-intro.mp4"
  outro "/assets/video/act-iii-outro.mp4"
  inventory compass stamp
  caption "Quill rows. I hold the compass. Neither of us mentions the flag on the wreck, so we both look at it instead."
  on start
    say "On the coral, Quill fishes something out of the bilge and holds it up by one end: my crowbar. “You packed a crowbar.” A pause. “Of course you did.” She drops it in my lap."
    give crowbar

act 4 "All Hands Returned"
  start dock at 880,830
  intro "/assets/video/act-iv-intro.mp4"
  outro "/assets/video/act-iv-outro.mp4"
  inventory compass stamp crowbar ansel_log
  caption "Port Vela, that same night. Cray's cutter got home first. At the dawn bell he means to write us all down as lost, and this time he's holding the pen."
  on start
    talk quill4

ending "ALL HANDS RETURNED"
  title if ending_pirate
    "THE PURSER OF THE MARROW"
  title if ending_desk
    "THE HONEST LEDGER"
  # the pirate ending: dawn from the crow's nest
  line if ending_pirate
    "Dawn, from the Marrow's crow's nest. Quill points. “That's the Liar. It moves.” “I'll write it down.” “You do that.”"
  line if ending_pirate and aff >= 14
    "Her hand is in mine before the Liar has even set. Neither of us writes that down."
  line if ending_pirate and not (aff >= 14)
    "She kissed me once, on a salt pan, and has since filed it under heatstroke. She stands close enough to amend the record."
  line if ending_pirate
    "My father's compass sits in the Marrow's binnacle. Quill steers by it and pretends she doesn't need to. It still points at the Old Nail. So, most days, do we."
  line if ending_pirate
    "I brought Bramwick his stamp. He gave me a smaller one from his drawer: PURSER, THE MARROW. He'd had it cut that morning, before I'd decided."
  line if ending_pirate
    "Flag sixteen flies at the masthead. It's mustard. My mother would have hated it."
  # the desk ending: the customs-house window, a year on
  line if ending_desk
    "A year later, at the customs-house window: a sail on the horizon, a patchwork flag at her masthead. I stamp her ARRIVED before she's even rounded the light."
  line if ending_desk and aff >= 14
    "She comes up the quay at a run, as she does every season, with a new star for me. I've written down four. One of them moves."
  line if ending_desk and aff >= 14 and night_watch
    "Every one of them is underlined."
  line if ending_desk and aff >= 14
    "On the quay she calls me cargo. On the steps, where nobody's counting, she doesn't."
  line if ending_desk and not (aff >= 14)
    "She still calls me cargo. She said my name once, across a harbour, and is rationing the rest. Every season she brings a star and lets me write it down."
  line if ending_desk
    "I gave Quill the compass. It points at the Old Nail, which lines up the Needle, which leads here. She has never once been late."
  line if ending_desk
    "Bramwick moved my desk six inches nearer the window. He says it's regulation. He wrote it that morning."
  # the epilogue, for both
  line
    "Quill was named navigator of the Marrow. She had it written into the articles, then read out, then read out again."
  line
    "Captain Vane's storm claim was paid at last, with three years' interest. She uses the letter as a bookmark."
  line
    "My father opened a shop on the quay. Every compass in it points at the Old Nail, and is useless anywhere else. He says that isn't a fault. It's how you find your way home."
  line
    "Rook works the counter in my father's shop. He tests every compass himself, sober, and the two of them argue about the reef until closing. Neither has ever let the other win."
  line if wager and iou_paid
    "Bramwick and Marta were married in the spring, paid for by a betting slate and a clerk who backed the right ship."
  line if wager and not iou_paid
    "My winnings off the betting slate went into a jar behind the Salty Keel's bar, labelled WEDDING, IF HE EVER PAYS UP. It is filling nicely. So, slowly, is his courage."
  line if iou_paid and not wager
    "Bramwick and Marta are still playing for it, one hand a night. He loses on purpose. She lets him think she can't tell."
  line if not iou_paid and not wager
    "Bramwick and Marta are still playing for it, after a fashion. The IOU is in his breast pocket, unpaid, and she has stopped pretending she doesn't know which pocket."
  line
    "Marta tells the whole story every night at nine, every word, and charges for the ending. Nobody has ever been allowed to skip to it."
  line
    "Old Onn never swept that step again. Tam ran out of wall and started on the lighthouse. He's up to a hundred and thirty, and one ship."
  line
    "Hobb's other arm is filling up nicely. He's put me on it, spelled wrong, which I'm told is an honour."
  line
    "Pike is junior clerk at the customs house. He dates everything, including the cat. Bramwick says it's the first time in thirty years the ledger has known what day it is."
  line if kelp_read
    "The last of Cray's kelp went on the Salty Keel's fire. For a week the whole harbour smelled of fog, and laughed."
  line if kelp_proof and not kelp_read
    "I kept the kelp manifest. FOR FOG. Nobody else ever read it out, and on very clear days I read it to myself."
  line if silas_refused
    "Cray asked for my compass once more, through the bars, very politely. I said no. It runs in the family."
  line if ending_desk
    "Silas Cray appealed from his cell, in triplicate. They crossed my desk. I stamped all three RECEIVED: SURPLUS TO REQUIREMENTS."
  line if ending_pirate
    "Silas Cray appealed from his cell, in triplicate. Nib filed all three in pigeonhole one, unread. It's where things go to be safe."
  line
    "ARCADIA: returned. All hands."
